{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And she spoke.</b> דִּבּוּר everywhere is nothing but harsh speech, and so it says, ״The man, the lord of the land, spoke harshly with us״ (Genesis 42). And אֲמִירָה everywhere is nothing but language of supplication, and so it says, ״And he said: Please, my brothers, do not act wickedly״ (Genesis 19), ״And he said: Please hear my words״ (verse 6) — every נָא is language of request (Sifrei)." "<b>And Miriam and Aharon spoke.</b> She opened with speech first — therefore Scripture puts her first. And from where did Miriam know that Mosheh had separated from the woman? Rabbi Natan says: Miriam was beside Tziporah when it was said to Mosheh, Eldad and Medad are prophesying in the camp. When Tziporah heard, she said: Woe to the wives of these men, if they are required for prophecy — they will be separating from their wives just as my husband separated from me. From there Miriam knew and told it to Aharon. And if Miriam, who did not intend to disparage him, was punished thus — how much more so one who tells the disparagement of his fellow (Sifrei)." "<b>The Cushite woman.</b> This tells that everyone acknowledged her beauty, just as everyone acknowledges the blackness of a Cushite (there)." "<b>Cushite.</b> By gematria: יְפַת מַרְאֶה [beautiful of appearance]." "<b>On account of the woman.</b> Concerning her being sent away." "<b>For a Cushite woman he had taken.</b> What does the verse teach? Rather, you may have a woman who is beautiful in her looks but not beautiful in her deeds, or beautiful in her deeds but not in her looks — but this one is beautiful in everything." "<b>The Cushite woman.</b> On account of her beauty she is called Cushite — like a person who calls his handsome son Cushite, so that the evil eye should not gain dominion over him." "<b>For a Cushite woman he had taken.</b> And now he had divorced her."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:37.367369137Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}